# Ford v2 blocks

v2 blocks and styling fields live under `src/lib/blocks/v2`. They are **independent** of `src/lib/fields/layout-field` (v1 Section/Row).

## Styling fields

- Add layout via factories from `@/lib/blocks/v2` (`PaddingField`, `MarginField`, `InsetField`, `GapField`, `DisplayField`, `PositionField`, `ContainerField`, `OverflowField`, `VisibilityField`, `ColorField`, or `StyleFields`).
- Application field chrome defaults belong in `src/lib/blocks/v2/theme.ts` (units, linked, container).
- Per-block padding/margin amounts: `defineV2BlocksConfig({ sectionBlock: { padding: { mobile: { top: '1' } } } })` from `payload.config.ts`, and pass `block: 'sectionBlock'` to `StyleFields`.
- Call-site field `defaults` / `defaultValue` still override.
- Frontend: `applyStyles` / `applyPadding` (etc.) with an optional `slot`. Do not reuse `.section-layout-*` classes.
- Admin fields must stay compact (Better Editor inspector). Reuse `components/ui` (breakpoint tabs, box editor, segmented control).
- New fields: follow workspace skill `eagle-v2-styling-fields`.

## Blocks

- Colocate Payload config + render component under `src/lib/blocks/v2/<name>-block/`.
- Do not register a v2 block in v1 `section-block/blockRefs.ts` unless the task explicitly mounts it there.
- Always add `admin.images.icon` + `admin.images.thumbnail` (3:2 PNG + square SVG under `public/blocks/`). Follow workspace skill `creating-block-admin-images` and match `heading-block-thumbnail.png` / `section-inner-block-thumbnail.png` style.
